  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nModel soundings show plenty of moisture today with precipitable\nwater values of 1.75 to 2 inches. Effective layer CAPE is\ngenerally in the 1700 to 2500 range. Those values combined with\nstorm motions under 10 knots lead to the potential for flash\nflooding this afternoon and evening. \n\nModel CAPE values drop some on Tuesday with storm motions \nincreasing slightly, even though precipitable water remains\nhigh. Can't rule out some localized flash flooding, although\nthreat is a bit lower than today. \n\nWith changes of showers and thunderstorms through the week and \nsome areas becoming saturated, localized flash flooding\ncontinues to be a possibility. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\n\nMoisture remains over the area through the work week and into\nthe next weekend. This will allow for showers and thunderstorms\neach day, more numerous in the afternoon and evening hours. \n\nSome dry air does slip in aloft on Wednesday, but plenty of\nmoisture remains in the lower levels. This could lead to some\nstronger storms producing damaging winds Wednesday afternoon \nand evening.",
